# Template for .env.secret (gitignored), read by `pnpm release` and `pnpm build:install`. Local installation
# uses only APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY; release signing modes are in apps/desktop/README.md's "Release builds" section.
# Values may be bare or in one layer of matching quotes, so spaces are fine. There is no `$VAR` or `~` expansion:
# write paths out in full. A trailing `# note` on a value line is part of the value.
# Notarization with an Apple ID (APPLE_ID, APPLE_PASSWORD) is not supported: `pnpm release` refuses it, so drop
# those lines from an older file.

# The "Developer ID Application" certificate can only be created on the developer portal's web form, by the
# Account Holder: the API (`POST /v1/certificates`) answers 403 to a team key however much access it has. The
# form's Sub-CA selector defaults to "Previous Sub-CA", whose certificates all expire on 2027-02-01, so pick "G2
# Sub-CA" by hand. After importing the certificate and its private key, also import the Developer ID G2
# intermediate (https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/DeveloperIDG2CA.cer): without it the chain cannot be
# built and `security find-identity` keeps reporting "0 valid identities found".

# The "Developer ID Application" certificate's name, the quoted part of the matching line of
# `security find-identity -v -p codesigning` without the quotes. Not the hash, not an "Apple Development" line.
#   APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY=Developer ID Application: Your Name (ABCDE12345)
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY=

# Notarization, through an App Store Connect API key: the key's 10-character ID, the issuer UUID shown above the key
# list, and the absolute path of the downloaded .p8
#   APPLE_API_KEY=ABCDE12345
#   APPLE_API_ISSUER=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#   APPLE_API_KEY_PATH=/Users/you/keys/AuthKey_ABCDE12345.p8
APPLE_API_KEY=
APPLE_API_ISSUER=
APPLE_API_KEY_PATH=
